.TH R_MEMPOOL_REALLOC_ENTRY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
r_mempool_realloc_entry \- reallocate an entry to a different size
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cmempool.h>

void *r_mempool_realloc_entry(r_mempool *rmp, void *addr, size_t size);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Changes the size of an allocated entry. If the new size maps to the same
pool as the old size, returns the original pointer. Otherwise, allocates
a new entry, copies min(old_size, new_size) bytes, and frees the old entry.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
rmp   Ranged memory pool
addr  Existing entry to reallocate, or NULL to allocate new
size  New size in bytes (must be > 0 and <= largest_size)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns pointer to reallocated entry on success
Returns NULL on failure
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
If addr is NULL, equivalent to r_mempool_alloc_entry()
If new size maps to same pool, returns original pointer (no copy)
Otherwise, allocates new, copies data, frees old
Copies min(old_user_size, new_user_size) bytes
Old entry is automatically freed if reallocation succeeds
Thread-safe if pool created with single_threaded=false
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR r_mempool_alloc_entry (3),
.BR r_mempool_free_entry (3)
